              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Armed with sword, thrusting spear, javelins and shield. May have light armour (+2 pts). Light Infantry. Stubborn. 0-1 unit; up to eight figures per 1,000 pts of the army. The self-proclaimed King Antiochus who led the first slave revolt had a bodyguard of his fellow Syrians; assumed equipped somewhat as Seleucid Thureophoroi. First Sicilian Slave Revolt only. (Spartacus p.42)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="93a9-0067-bec4-650f" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
