  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="0ee3-33a4-a237-720d" name="Sicilian Slave Revolt (Spartacus) - List Notes" publicationId="eb14-e889-c793-0fc4" hidden="false">
      <description>SICILIAN SLAVE REVOLT ARMY LIST (Spartacus, pp.42-43). Designed to help you create a Slave army from the first two major revolts in Sicily, or any other civil rebellion or large-scale banditry in this period. Roman opponents for the early Servile wars: the Republican lists in Armies of Antiquity (Levies or Velites may exchange their throwing spear for a sling) or the Late Republican Consular Roman army (note that Lucullus raised many conscript troops; for the Second Sicilian revolt increase the points of Auxiliary and Support troops to 35%).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Sicilian Slave Revolt - First Sicilian Slave Revolt]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Slave Infantry: at least 60%
  Cavalry: up to 15%
  Characters up to 25%, Infantry at least 60% (includes special units), Cavalry up to 15% (none are available in this revolt). The First Sicilian Slave Revolt army may have Antiochus's bodyguard and packs of dogs. They may not have any cavalry or bandit units. The Slave units may not take pilum or large shield (its main leaders were Eunus/Antiochus and Kleon).
[Sicilian Slave Revolt - Titus Minutius]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Slave Infantry: at least 60%
  Cavalry: up to 15%
  Characters up to 25%, Infantry at least 60%. Titus Minutius's army may have up to two Trained Slave units (his revolt was the only one planned and he obtained some armour prior to the revolt starting, plus he organized his men into centuries). Players may not take Cavalry, Bandits or Dogs.
[Sicilian Slave Revolt - Second Sicilian Slave Revolt]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Slave Infantry: at least 60%
  Cavalry: up to 15%
  Characters up to 25%, Infantry at least 60%, Cavalry up to 15%. The Second Sicilian Slave Revolt army may have Cavalry and Bandits but may not take Bodyguards or Dogs (its main leaders were Salvius/'King' Tryphon and Athenion).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
